## P0 — IMMEDIATE: Gemini transport recovery without wrapper interference

The provider's generation and stream must be allowed to finish. Do not redesign streaming modes or make agent features depend on streamed text callbacks. Limit changes to Gemini transport recovery and duplicate-text suppression.

- [x] Remove the Agent-specific retry-warning branch; all providers use the normal `GenerateStream` interface when a text sink is active.
- [x] Do not abort a Gemini generation just because visible text has started. Retry recoverable transport interruptions up to the existing attempt limit.
- [x] On a replayed generation, suppress the exact visible text prefix and stream only the new suffix. Do not display retry-attempt warnings.
- [x] Accept a completed text response when a Gemini-compatible endpoint closes cleanly without `finishReason`.
- [x] Add an Agent regression: with streamed text enabled, a returned `write_file` function call still executes once, its result enters the follow-up model request, and the final answer streams normally. The text callback is presentation-only; Agent logic consumes the completed `Content` response.
- [ ] Verify every non-Gemini provider retains its own native `GenerateStream` path; do not route them through Gemini retry handling.
- [ ] Run `gofmt`, `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and the Linux amd64 build on `work`. Fix all failures before moving to lower-priority work.
- [ ] Run real Gemini streaming smoke tests: normal long response, partial response followed by a simulated transport interruption, tool/function call, and final response. Confirm there is no duplicated visible prefix and no lost output.

